the unions have accused the health  secretary of being afraid to debate the  issues raised by the new contract they  accuse him of forcing this one down  their throats we go to Westminster in  the Health Secretary Jeremy Hunt is  there with us this morning good morning  to you secretary good morning Erin  not somebody could die today if so  you've got to take some of the  responsibility haven't you well the  people who are responsible for what has  happened today are the people who are  choosing to strike striking withdrawing  emergency care as you say for the first  time in NHS history is a choice and all  I would say is that we have had huge  discussions over how we deliver a  seven-day NHS we've been having them now  for over three years we've had 75  meetings but you can disagree with what  the government's trying to do we say  that you can't choose which day of the  week you're ill and that's why we want  to promise every NHS in fairness second  estate they're saying you're trying to  deliver a seven-day NHS with five day  resources yes well that's not true  because this year we're actually putting  into the NHS the sixth biggest increase  in funding in its history but what we  know is that if you're going to improve  the NHS it isn't just about money it's  also about making sure that care  actually gets better for patients and as  I say you can disagree with the  government's vision for a seven-day NHS  but is it proportionate or appropriate  to withdraw emergency care from  vulnerable patients because that's  what's happening today the single issue  that we couldn't agree on where the  deadlock was was over Saturday pay and  we are offering doctors higher premium  for Saturday pay their nurses and  paramedics than the assistants who work  in their own operating theatres this is  a very fair deal and the question on  many people's mind is given that given  that you know police officers and fire  officers don't get any premium at all  for working at the we keep talking about  money right how much money we're talking  about how much money you're going to see  if by not paying them  what they want on a Saturday for  instance well we are paying them more  what they're actually getting on a  Saturday depending on the time of day as  time in a third or time-and-a-half so  we're not saying if you work regularly  on Saturday that we're not going to pay  more but the reality is that we can only  pay them at levels that mean that we can  afford to have proper medical cover at  weekends you'll be saying all the ways  you could save money in the NHS of all  the the people you could club I mean if  you were going after the pharmaceutical  companies who were making massive  profits over over medicines and things  people may say well done people don't  want you to be clubbing doctors do they  well and we're not and you know as you  know perfectly well 75% of doctors will  actually see their pay go up under the  new contract and the doctors pay bill  will not be going down it'll be going up  but what we're saying is that you know  the first line on the first page of our  manifesto was a seven-day NHS in the  general election we had last year and  that is because you know if we are going  to offer high-quality care in the NHS we  want to be able to promise every patient  it doesn't matter which day of the week  you get ill you can't control that but  you can be confident of the same high  quality care from your NHS that's  something that's overwhelmingly  supported by the public but we have a  duty now to deliver that manifesto  promise and a no Union however powerful  however popular has a right to veto a  manifesto promise that the British  people are voted for so this is not  about money this is not about principle  this is not about medicine this is about  politics now this is about some  manifesto that you've had I mean this is  you against the union's then well I'm  sorry but you can't dismiss the  manifesto and say it's just about  politics a manifesto is what political  parties promised before elections and  what would you be saying to me in a  year's time or two years time if I was  on this program and I said I'm really  sorry I didn't deliver what we promised  in our manifesto because it was a little  bit difficult at the time and the  doctors union didn't like it you would  accept that wait so you made a promise  to the British people no we made this  promise for a tell seven day and age  and we have a duty if properly funded I  suppose but see how I said to you we're  putting okay huge amounts of extra  planning I mean there's 3.8 billion  pounds yes of extra funding going into  the NHS this year but I have met too  many patients who've told me  heartbreaking stories of tragedies that  they and their families have suffered  because they didn't get the care that  they needed at we say having more junior  doctors at the weekend would would stop  that but you have to have the ancillary  services as well exactly and that's what  I said in my statement yesterday that  this isn't just about junior doctors  it's about consultants is about  seven-day diagnostic services it's about  seven-day access to the social care  system it's about seven-day GP services  it's about a whole range of services to  make sure that NHS patients often we're  out of time they get we're heading  towards the break just some concern  about you are you running the show still  are you still in charge here the fact  that we're talking about politics are  you being told what to do by the prime  minister or is this your ballgame the  Prime Minister owner how are absolutely  at one that our solemn responsibility is  to deliver what we promise to the  British people we would do and that is a  seven-day NHS so they can be confident  in their NHS care every day of the week  health secretary thank you for your time  this morning we're not just over half an  hour away from this Oh like strike  appreciate your time thank you we have  to leave it there thank you very much  indeed as a Secretary of State for  Health Jeremy Hunt there's a Sky News  sunrise on a Tuesday back after this

